+## Hosted page feedback
+
+`COMMENTS_ENABLED=true` enables the native comments link/lookup integration for public HTML pages. It is disabled when omitted. This is an adapter to hosted MarkLayer; deploying Energon does not deploy a MarkLayer backend. The widget is a pinned, versioned asset served by Energon, while comments and uploads remain at `https://marklayer.app`.
+
+Normal publish APIs and clean URLs keep their behavior. `?comments=1` resolves or creates one shared current room; `?comments=new` starts a team-authorized confirmation flow with a compact dialog over a sandboxed, noninteractive preview of the clean page; the URL temporarily moves to the hub and the preview reloads, so existing scroll and application state are not preserved; `?comments=<room-id>` selects an existing round. Token agents use GET/POST `/v1/comments`. Room lookup is read-only; creation uses normal page write authority. Protect the existing content-host sandbox and keep transformed responses out of the raw-body cache. Password/private pages, Markdown, assets, downloads, and export/API byte reads do not gain widgets.
+
+Recognized existing comments embeds are refused with `409 comments_already_embedded` before provisioning. Existing unflagged prototype pages keep their original behavior; use their original URL or remove the embed before enabling this integration. A renamed standalone HTML file requires a room matching its new canonical URL; lookup reports none until ensure prepares it.
+
+The pinned frontend excludes editable fields from selection capture and uses the existing adopted-stylesheet mechanism for controls and loading errors, preserving authored CSP. Expired concrete reviews keep their round identity and offer explicit current-review navigation; temporary failures retry the same room. Known-missing associations show that recovery immediately without a hosted request. No provider probe is added to ordinary concrete page serving.
+
+The room lookup is local metadata; it is not a backup of comments. Hosted anonymous rooms follow MarkLayer's 90-day inactivity cleanup. Setting Energon content retention to never does not change that policy, and existing hosted room links do not inherit later Energon permission changes. Do not use hosted feedback for protected content. Disabling this integration stops Energon from adding controls or exposing its lookup; it does not delete hosted feedback or revoke room links already shared.
+
+Optional reviewer-name memory uses MarkLayer's native identity storage adapter. Provision a dedicated random `COMMENTS_IDENTITY_SECRET` (at least 32 characters) with `wrangler secret put COMMENTS_IDENTITY_SECRET`; never reuse an API token or put it in source. Without it the widget retains ordinary commenting without cross-link memory. Apply migration `0029_comment_identities.sql` before enabling this feature. Eligible final review documents alone establish a host-only, Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax browser cookie and receive private/no-store identity bootstrap data. Clean pages remain unchanged. The cookie lives for 90 days from creation; saved preferences and Forget tombstones expire 90 days after the explicit change and are removed by the existing cron. No row is created by bootstrap, typing, Back, or Skip.
+
+The internal content-host `/comments/identity` resource accepts only a scoped one-hour bearer capability for a name save or explicit Forget; sandbox requests omit credentials. Capabilities contain neither the browser cookie nor account authority and retain their original deadline after writes. Random record revisions reject stale saves even after expiry and recreation; explicit Forget wins across tabs without rewriting MarkLayer comments. An expired capability or unavailable preference storage must not block feedback: the name works for the current review, and reopening the review obtains a fresh capability. Org-write installations with restricted publisher email domains share name preferences only across publishers whose current account still belongs to an allowed domain; open or owner-write installations and unproven or outside-domain owners scope preferences to the page owner. The browser cookie identifies a preference, not an authenticated person.
+
+Keep comments schema migrations additive and apply them before the Worker. Retain the previous pinned widget assets through rollback. A rollback to a Worker without comments restores plain serving while leaving authored content and hosted rooms untouched. Verify clean/review views, current/new lookup, shared comments across two browsers, selected text/pins, agent reads, and protected-page exclusion with `.agents/skills/verify-energon/features/comments.md` before promotion.
+
+Runtime discovery (`/v1/help`, hub `/llms.txt`, and the gateway OpenAPI document) updates with the Worker. Existing token and publishing commands remain valid. Render the publish plugin from `templates/` with `npm run skill:render`, publish that generated package through the deployment repository, and refresh installed clients through the existing marketplace procedure in INSTALL.md. An already-imported gateway schema must be refreshed to gain `comments.getComments` and `comments.createCommentReview`; no replacement token is needed. Agents with an older local skill can follow the live discovery documents immediately.
+
+The public review query parameter also accepts `comment` and `feedback` as aliases for `comments`, with identical values and authorization. Bare or empty values activate the current review just like `comments=1`. Generated links remain plural. Mixed or repeated mode parameters are rejected as ambiguous.
diff --git a/docs/solutions/database-issues/cold-isolate-bootstrap-latency.md b/docs/solutions/database-issues/cold-isolate-bootstrap-latency.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1dad04d9e5f1355373e70c333d0e467c138f00bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/solutions/database-issues/cold-isolate-bootstrap-latency.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Repeated cold-isolate bootstrap stalls content reads
+
+A correlated production trace showed 6.7 seconds of schema initialization and
+legacy R2-prefix scans before the content read began. Individual D1 SQL execution
+was sub-millisecond; serial binding round trips dominated. Isolate-local flags
+cannot establish that a database/storage upgrade has already completed elsewhere.
+
+`bootstrap_state` records separate runtime completion receipts for schema
+initialization and the pre-id R2 migration. SQL migration 0027 only creates the
+receipt table. Runtime writes a receipt only after the corresponding work
+succeeds. Missing-table errors allow fresh databases to initialize; other errors
+propagate. In-flight promises coalesce work within one isolate and retry failures;
+they are not cross-isolate locks. The existing cross-isolate migration semantics
+are unchanged.
+
+When changing runtime schema or backfills, bump `SCHEMA_REVISION` in `src/db.ts`.
+Do not seed receipts merely because SQL migrations have run. The schema receipt
+is checked on each call, so a database reset does not inherit isolate readiness.
+The R2 receipt assumes the deployment keeps its dedicated database and bucket
+paired and that current writers use id/version keys. A restore of pre-id objects
+or a rollback to pre-id writers requires an explicit recovery plan for the R2
+receipt; do not reuse it to certify newly restored legacy data.
+
+No authorization, expiry, cache policy, URL, or content-serving code changes are
+needed. Tests cover fresh/0005-shaped upgrades, stale revisions, restart skips,
+concurrent initialization, narrow error handling, failed R2 work and retries.
+
+## Deferred ownership after schema completion
+
+A legacy database may finish schema bootstrap before its creators have user
+records. `ensureUser` attaches still-unowned sites, loose files, and tokens
+matching the resolved email. New-user insertion and attachment share a D1
+transaction; existing users are repaired by an idempotent batch. Attach before
+retiring or changing an email so a replacement IdP subject cannot inherit the
+previous identity's deferred content. Never overwrite an assigned owner.
+
+This work runs during identity resolution, not public content reads. Keep the
+schema and R2 receipts intact: do not rerun bootstrap to repair ownership.
+`test/legacy-ownership.spec.ts` exercises a migration-0005-shaped database,
+late and previously completed logins, identity transitions, retry, and a fresh
+binding that skips schema work after completion.
